    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, can you explain the mechanism of action for ACE inhibitors like Lisinopril? I'm trying to understand specifically how they interact with the RAAS pathway to help lower blood pressure for my boards. Thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "ACE inhibitors like lisinopril block the enzyme angiotensin-converting enzyme, preventing the conversion of angiotensin I to the potent vasoconstrictor angiotensin II. By inhibiting this step, they also reduce aldosterone secretion from the adrenal glands, leading to decreased sodium and water reabsorption in the kidneys. This dual mechanism reduces systemic vascular resistance and blood volume, effectively lowering blood pressure.",
      "source": "target",
